  "answer_text": "To quantify the impact of room light, you need to compare a measurement taken with the laser on (the \"normal\" spectrum) against a measurement where no signal other than potential background/leakage is present. By using `acquire_spectrum` with `shutter='close'`, you can capture a \"dark\" frame which contains only electronic noise and any ambient light leakage from the room. Comparing these two measurements allows you to identify the magnitude of the shared components (the broad, unwanted signal). To then isolate the pure sample signal for analysis, you subtract the dark frame's intensity from the normal measurement's intensity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plan\": [\n    \"acquire_spectrum\",\n    \"acquire_spectrum\",\n    \"run_analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"decision\": \"normal_minus_dark\"\n}\n```",
